/*!
\page page_gettingstarted Getting started

Before we start    {#sec_installation_requirements}
===============

To install and use the VEF you will need to satisfy the following requirements:
-# Python version 2.7.X installed. 
-# Python packages installed: numpy, scipy and matplotlib.


\note If you are not familiar with [Python](https://www.python.org/), the easiest way to get it installed is to download 
[Miniconda Python distribution](http://conda.pydata.org/miniconda.html). Once it is installed,
you may run the following command from the command line to get the required packages:
<pre class="consoleView">
conda install numpy scipy matplotlib -y
</pre>


Installation and configuration    {#sec_installation}
==============================

You received the archive file VEF_verXXX_yyyymmdd.zip, which contains the distribution of the VEF binaries, scripts, examples and documentation. 
This instruction will tell you step-by-step how to install and set-up the VEF software on your Windows computer.


-# Unpack the distribution to a directory you prefer, for example: `c:\VEF` or `c:\Users\<i>your-user_name<i>\VEF`. 
   Note: the path to that directory should not contain spaces.
-# Edit the VEF configuration file \fsname{vef.cmd}, located in the directory where you unpacked the distribution. 
   You will need to customize the line that sets \envname{VEF_ROOT} by setting it to the path where the VEF is unpacked. 
   For example:
   \verbatim
   set VEF_ROOT="c:\VEF"
   \endverbatim
   or, if you unpacked the VEF distribution to your home directory:
   \verbatim
   set VEF_ROOT="%USERPROFILE%\VEF"
   \endverbatim

   
Setting up the simulations with HMS    {#sec_setting_up_simulation}
===================================

The VEF programs are run from the command line. In order to conduct any VEF simulation, you have to configure VEF environment first. 
It is as simple as running \fsname{vef.cmd} before starting any VEF program. 
For example:
\verbatim
c:\VEF\vef.cmd
\endverbatim

\note You have to run \fsname{vef.cmd} at the beginning of every VEF session.

*/
